    llvm_backend_yield_silent_noop_2026-07-19, 1, "2026-11-10 scoped FIXED: PR8120 merged as 5c089d25fa6459d89fd07e063edee2c8b411977b. Original Expected explicitly permits a hard LLVM compile error instead of generator lowering. Rust LLVM MirInst::Yield now returns the generator-unsupported diagnostic, including direct MIR callers bypassing fallback. Real LLVM backend tests llvm_yield_refusal_errors_on_x86_and_x64 and llvm_yield_refusal_preserves_ordinary_return executed 2 passed / 0 failed / 0 ignored; negative x86/x64 refusal and positive optimized verified nonempty ordinary object. Reviewed/executed functions.rs SHA256 b8e16335874973dbffae92c2a4942dab0aa67e3f4521d874e86d02fae03f16ec matches merged source. Test executable SHA256 69afbc7e1c0e4952e59a1a015b8b40da31aaa2635f42f00aebc001776cac59a1. Astra exact-source review PASS and CI green recorded for PR8120. This closes only Rust LLVM silent Yield dropping; no generator implementation, pure-Simple backend, self-hosted CLI/runtime, ActorSend/ActorReply, optional legacy suite or related async qualification. Historical description and triage are retained as baseline. Tracker reconciliation reruns no backend tests. Evidence: llvm_backend_yield_silent_noop_2026-07-19.md."
